From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Stoffel <stoffel.thomas.ryan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:41:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] workbench: load wisp's contribution from the desktop main

src/vs/workbench/contrib/wisp/browser/wisp.contribution.ts comes from the
overlay and is wisp's entry point in the workbench. It registers wisp's
default settings in code, so they apply from the first launch: a
built-in extension's configurationDefaults reach startup only through a
cache written on an earlier run.

For now it turns on upstream's chat.disableAIFeatures, which hides the
Chat and Copilot entry points that the registration filter leaves in
place. wisp's own workbench code, such as the coordinator view, can be
imported from the same file without another patch.

The import goes last in the desktop main, after every upstream
contribution it adjusts.

diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/workbench.desktop.main.ts b/src/vs/workbench/workbench.desktop.main.ts
index a02eb91a007b0c338b7b8916452fd029756c6e87..952de0de92e7eda95b628020c9e287283dce7758 100644
--- a/src/vs/workbench/workbench.desktop.main.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/workbench.desktop.main.ts
@@ -210,6 +210,9 @@ import './contrib/keybindingsExport/electron-browser/keybindingsExport.contribut
 // System-wide (OS global) Keybindings
 import './contrib/keybindings/electron-browser/systemWideKeybindings.contribution.js';
 
+// wisp
+import './contrib/wisp/browser/wisp.contribution.js';
+
 //#endregion
 
 
